# Coordinate + geometry probe for DESK31/32/33/38.
#
# probe_patch.py's `probe_dump()` prints the menu bar, every drop-down box and
# every entry with its absolute rectangle; that is where DESK32's measured cell
# widths come from (box ob_width / 8 px per character cell).  `probe_icons()`
# prints every desktop icon and every window item with the point that hits it;
# that is where every click coordinate below and in the other lists comes from.
#
# The run: idle desktop (both dumps), then open the C:\ window by double-
# clicking the C: drive icon (the dumps again, now with the window items), then
# hover each of the four menu titles in turn.
200 parkbr
1000 arm
1100 mark A_IDLE
1500 move 37 42
1700 down
1703 up
1710 down
1713 up
2300 move 600 240
3000 mark B_WIN1
3400 move 20 8
3800 mark C_DESK_OPEN
4200 move 68 8
4600 mark D_FILE_OPEN
5000 move 116 8
5400 mark E_VIEW_OPEN
5800 move 172 8
6200 mark F_OPTIONS_OPEN
6600 parkbr
7000 mark G_END
